# Push after every ask

When Dustin’s request is done, if this repo has uncommitted or unpushed work from that request:

1. Stage the relevant files (do not commit secrets).
2. Create a commit following the existing message style (focus on why).
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`).
4. If HTTPS fails with OpenSSL issuer errors, retry with `git -c http.sslBackend=schannel push origin HEAD` without changing git config.

Do this even if he did not say “commit” or “push” in that message. Skip only when there is nothing to commit or push.
